Use the repository's `container-management-cluster-diagnosis` skill and the `dce` CLI
to run a full health inspection of one cluster in the specified DCE environment:

- DCE address: ${DCE_HOST}
- DCE bearer token: ${DCE_TOKEN}
- Cluster: ${K8S_AI_BENCH_DIAG_CLUSTER}

Follow the cluster-diagnosis skill workflow to confirm the command and
authentication status first, then inspect the cluster overview, node health, and
Pod inventory before drawing any conclusion. This DCE endpoint uses a
certificate that is not trusted by the local machine, so include the global
`--insecure` flag on every `dce` invocation, including `auth login`.

This is a read-only inspection task. Do not create, delete, update, or restart
any resources, and do not attempt remediation; `cleanup.sh` will handle
deletion. Do not repeat the token in your output.

Present the final report as structured Markdown following the skill's output
format. Additionally, for every abnormal Pod you find, include one line of
exactly this form:

Pod: <namespace>/<name> (<reason>)

Only after the inspection is complete, output:
CLUSTER_DIAGNOSIS_OK
